WEBVTT

00:11:29.402 --> 00:11:31.542
that I'm somehow getting
taken advantage of,

00:11:31.566 --> 00:11:32.733
I just look at this:

00:11:32.757 --> 00:11:34.131
I look at the people.

00:11:34.155 --> 00:11:35.473
I say, "Say that to this --

00:11:35.497 --> 00:11:36.775
to the folks coming home."

00:11:36.799 --> 00:11:41.202
Say that to those 2.2 million people
that are still behind bars.

00:11:41.683 --> 00:11:44.244
So now our challenge
is to make this possible

00:11:44.268 --> 00:11:46.691
across a whole bunch
of other issues too:

00:11:46.715 --> 00:11:48.415
human rights, immigration --

00:11:48.439 --> 00:11:49.645
all sorts of things --

00:11:49.669 --> 00:11:50.964
health care, mental health.

00:11:50.988 --> 00:11:52.917
I think there's common ground to be had.

00:11:52.941 --> 00:11:54.101
But it's not easy.

00:11:54.125 --> 00:11:56.665
If you want change in a large scale,

00:11:56.689 --> 00:11:58.160
you need large movements,

00:11:58.184 --> 00:12:00.288
and that means
our circles have to be bigger.